00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:52,600
The rule is, and it says exactly this,

221
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:55,680
is a Scout can challenge any merit badge at any time.

222
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:59,760
So this is all in that wonderful handbook,

223
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:03,600
the Advancement Committee Policies and Procedures book.

224
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:07,860
And now, you don't get this book and run around like you'll

225
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:10,620
and point your finger in people's face and say,

226
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:14,180
So let it be written. So let it be done.

227
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,880
No. You use this to be helpful,

228
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,260
not to be a doctrinaire of fuss budget

229
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:23,560
who's going to go around and tell people the right way to do things.

230
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:26,480
I'm just telling you these things because they were great help to me.

231
00:19:26,919 --> 00:19:31,120
I'm not trying to put my nose into your business and say,

232
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,419
Well, you have to change all these things about your program.

233
00:19:33,919 --> 00:19:35,399
I'll let you take care of that.

234
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,360
You'll figure it out.

235
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:39,800
But these are pretty invaluable resources.

236
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:45,120
Now, there's a third one that is not yet a PDF file as of this recording,

237
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:48,280
but it is available online in its entirety,

238
00:19:48,479 --> 00:19:50,419
and that is the BSA Insignia Guide.

239
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,699
And it can be very helpful, too,

240
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:54,560
because there are questions that come up.

241
00:19:54,639 --> 00:19:56,199
There are questions that come up all the time

242
00:19:56,199 --> 00:19:59,580
about, you know, how this is worn and where this is put

243
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,020
and how many of these can I put on

244
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:03,479
and how many square knots can dance on the head of a pen.

245
00:20:03,939 --> 00:20:06,739
Well, turn to the Insignia Guide for your answers,

246
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:10,820
because in the Insignia Guide, as in all the other guides,

247
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:11,900
So let it be written.

248
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:14,340
So let it be done.

249
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:16,100
That's right.

250
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:21,280
If it's written in there, you can count on it being national policy.

251
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:24,140
If it's not in there and somebody tells you something different,

252
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:27,640
well, I would be kind of suspicious of that statement.

253
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:31,920
Three resources that will help you as a scout leader,

254
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:34,120
there are the Insignia Guide,

255
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:37,480
the Advancement Committee Policies and Procedures Guide,

256
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,680
and finally the Guide to Safe Scouting.

257
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:43,360
They're all three should be in any scout leader's possession,

258
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:46,740
either as a PDF file or you should be able to find it on the web.

259
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,880
Definitely save you a lot of time, folks.

260
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,360
And remember what Ewell said.

261
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:51,540
So let it be written.

262
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:53,960
So let it be done.

263
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:54,080
Thank you.

264
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:21,940
That's right.

265
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:25,140
It's time for a Scoutmaster's Minute.

266
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:35,580
A Scout is brave.

267
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:36,100
Yep.

268
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,940
A Scout can face danger.

269
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,600
He might be afraid, but he can still face it.

270
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:44,480
He has the courage to stand for what he thinks is right,

271
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:46,720
even if others laugh at him or threaten him.

272
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:49,500
That's real bravery in my book.

273
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,940
Chutzpah is a great old Yiddish word

274
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:58,140
that has been defined as a combination of gall and nerve and guts

275
00:21:58,140 --> 00:22:01,300
and presumption and arrogance.

276
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:08,860
I mean, it might not be as noble as the connotations that we attach to bravery.

277
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:13,580
And it may not be that all brave people have chutzpah,

278
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:18,740
but those with chutzpah, baby, they are brave in one way or another.

279
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:22,620
I mean, it takes real chutzpah to stand up to society.

280
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:27,320
Our Scouts win popularity or risk ostracism

281
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:29,760
at the shifting standards of their peers.

282
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,920
Do you remember that?

283
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:32,960
Remember?

284
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:36,960
One day one thing was cool and you go to school the next day

285
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:37,960
and it's not cool anymore?

286
00:22:39,140 --> 00:22:40,140
Hehehehe.

287
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:46,640
There's no more unforgiving and intense and capricious society

288
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:50,180
than the one we encounter when we're teenagers.

289
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:51,020
You know?

290
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:55,340
It takes chutzpah to be a scout in that society,

291
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:57,320
to stand out and to achieve

292
00:22:57,320 --> 00:23:02,760
in a world that often belittles anyone who dares to explore their own potential.

293
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:06,380
But we've got chutzpah, right?

294
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,240
Because a scout is brave.

